; Generated by c64-source. Edit the values here: generate keeps them.
; The switches of the build. Each switch is 0 or 1: change a value, then build again.
; The defaults give the clean program: copy protection, trainers, cheats and
; changes of a crack are 0, and the fixes of the releases are 1.
; generate adds a new switch with its default and removes a switch that the
; knowledge does not have. The build of a release does not read this file.

; Copy protection: off by default
PROTECTION = 0 ; on in MAM, TBC. $1e30-$1e30. Disk protection of the start-up: the start-up script (op 9 at $1e30) jumps to $3a43, which tests RAM at $8413 and reads track 1 sectors 1 and 2 with U1 commands. TBC put NOPs over the checks after the reads (the original bytes are in no release). MAM put NOPs over the reads too (CRACK_MAM). Off: the script ends at $1e30.

; Changes of a crack: off by default
CRACK_MAM  = 0 ; on in MAM. $0998-$09a0, $09fc-$0a05, $3a59-$3a87, $3a97-$3a97, $3aa2-$3aa2, $3aad-$3ab5, $3aca-$3acc. MAM: joystick and keyboard control, and its own removal of the disk protection. The IRQ calls MAM code at $0829 in the first page of the MAM file KOALAPAINTER ($0801-$08ff): that page is not in the program of the knowledge, so a MAM build needs that file.
CRACK_TBC  = 0 ; on in TBC. $4800-$4838. TBC: the joystick routine at $4800, which the TBC loader KP hooks into the IRQ in joystick mode. MAM ends at $47ff, so the bytes of the original program at $4800-$4838 are not known: without TBC, the build has zero bytes there.

; Start screen: on by default
START_SCREEN = 1 ; the loader shows the start screen and waits for a key or a fire button. 0 starts the program at once. Only the clean build has it: a release and LEFTOVERS = 1 have none

; Leftovers: off by default
LEFTOVERS = 0 ; 540 bytes in 16 files in leftovers/ that nothing uses. 1 builds them, so main.asm gives the bytes of the program. Each release has them. The loader never loads them
